        <item>
            <title>1.11.0</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:53:21 +0530</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>210</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.11.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
  <li>A new Security page lists apps with something Keel can prove: an update the developer marked critical, an update whose notes mention a security fix, an outdated Sparkle with published security advisories, an Electron version that no longer gets security fixes, and a signature Gatekeeper doesn&#x27;t accept. Each finding says where its evidence comes from.</li>
  <li>Security updates get a Security tag and come first on Updates.</li>
  <li>Automatic installs can be limited to security updates (Settings, Installing).</li>
  <li>Keel works all of this out on your Mac. The lists of affected versions come with Keel&#x27;s signed catalog, so they stay current without a new Keel, and nothing about your apps is sent anywhere.</li>
  <li>An app whose own updater installs its new version, such as Comet, no longer has a tick box on Updates, and Select all counts only apps Keel can update.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
